  "id": "steady-state",
  "term": "steady state",
  "definition": "In this context, steady state refers to the auditory steady-state response, especially at 40 Hz: a brain response to sound used as an established way to assess gamma-band neural synchronization. It is also thought to reflect the balance between excitation and inhibition in cortical microcircuits.",
